    "turn_text": "I think that is part of the issue. And I think we need to reform the H1B visa process that has been abused by these companies to bring in lower wage. But I don't think that's the only issue. And the reason I say that is because there's no reason they can't have some of the similar credentialing programs and job creation programs here in the United States. We just haven't been intentional about it. We have not said, OK, our goal is to get people in the United States credential paid and higher. And it's been a failure. I would argue both of our policy in not doing that and the tech companies, but there's no doubt that we have to reform. h1b visa process, but a lot of these companies rather have these people in the United States that could speak the language who are in the same time zone Who you know you don't have that. Yeah, I live in the Bay Area.",
