    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88927.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Well, Joe, look, I think he has done a fair amount. Remember, unemployment was almost at 7% when he took office, it's down to 3.6%. He's gotten us out of some very difficult times by passing the American rescue plan that people may not remember. But everyone got a check when he first got into office, and that helped grow the economy. He's passed the infrastructure bill. But I think he has to do more. Look, I'll say two things concretely he can do. I'm here in Chicago. I was meeting with steelworkers in Chicago yesterday. They say when they were growing up in the 80s, there's African-American steelworkers. They said they felt that there were more economic opportunities for them growing up in the 80s and 90s to get some of these jobs than they are today. There are less jobs because a lot of the steel plants having been shut down or closed, the southward to a steel plant being shut down and Gary and Deanna being downsized And they said, what we really need is someone innovative, imaginative, to produce new things in America and to have a massive investment, fast investment in production and creating new jobs and creating new industry across this country where the government can help. The government can say we're going to finance these new plants to make new steel, to make gigafactories, to make the products of the future, so we're not as dependent on China. And the president can be bolder in providing that capital and purchase agreements and trying to create these plants and faster about it. And I think that would resonate. The second thing is, I think you can do more on inflation. We ought to be mobilizing the National Guard to go out and help with the transport that's hurting some of the supply chains. You should convene a council And get people from the Department of Agriculture, Department of Energy, other areas and say, well, an industry and say, OK, what are we going to do? Where are the bottlenecks? What do I need to do to try to increase production? So I just think there has to be more urgency focus on the economy in general.",
