    "turn_text": "I mean, I think what people want is they, they understand it's a hard time, but they want a government in motion, a president saying, I am mobilizing this country to get the economy back, to get inflation down, and I'm waking up every morning, and I'm thinking about that. You know, something struck me, I was in a very concerning. I was with my Uber driver. I will forget where people are with my Uber driver. The young African-American is about 27 years older, listening to the hip hop. I said, so what do you think about the president? He said, well, yeah, I'm not voting for gas prices went up. Other things, I voted for him over Trump. I'm not going to vote for him again. And I was concerned when he said that. And he said, you guys, all you're talking about is Ukraine. And all you're thinking about is how to stand up for Ukraine. I think the president has done a tremendous job on Ukraine. I think the president deserves a lot of credit. But it struck me that we have to wake up every morning talking about first the Uber driver and how to make his life better. And what we're doing for him in a, in, in convinced the American people that 80% of our efforts are energetic, trying to get this economy back, moving, creating good paying jobs and, and lowering prices. And I don't think, I think there's a disconnect that energy isn't coming through from our government.",
