    "turn_text": "the balance show I could I try never to go on television and criticize the president overall I think he's done a Good job. But if we don't sound the alarm heading to the midterm, say we've got a change course, focus more on the economy, have greater urgency, do some bold things, then we're going to have a rude awakening in November. And so if you say to me, will you do everything possible for this president to get reelected? Absolutely. I'll be campaigning all over the country. Will you support this president? Say he's doing a good job? Absolutely. But am I going to keep quiet when I'm hearing on the streets and places I go, a discontent and economic anxiety. That would be a disservice. It would be a disservice for the country and to the Democratic Party. And the upshot of that is going to be a speaker, Kevin McCarthy. So that's why I'm saying we've got to push this president and the Congress to do a few big things before November.",
